+## A `beforeSession` that throws
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: `onError` runs with the session and the thrown error, the argument shape every other orchestrator failure delivers ([validated by: runs onError with the session and the thrown error when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- That throw still rejects the caller with the original error, and `afterSession` still runs, so a cleanup hook cannot assume the turn started: a throw from `beforeSession` means no later hook has run and the provider has not been called ([validated by: still rejects the caller and runs afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L69)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
